Hello,
I would like an intercept that is spatially varying. So the intercept : beta_0 =  b_0 + 𝑣_0i but  𝑣_0i not to be iid but to be spatially correlated with the matern structure (that is why I use the dmatern latent model). In normal iid cases I see from the documentation that I can find the posterior distribution of  beta_0 with  inla.make.lincombs. But when I use:

SimData <- inla.posterior.sample(n = 10000, fit_p)
Npar <- nrow(fit_p$summary.fixed)
# Extract regression parameters
vars <- rownames(fit_p$summary.fixed)
Betas_sim <- inla.posterior.sample.eval( vars  , SimData)

the Betas_sim  seems to contain simulations only for the fixed part of the intercept since I get only two coefficients (one for z and one for intercept). Is there a way to get a simulated  beta_0 for each location (loc)?

